Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/pds/tif_pdsdirwrite.c
Line: 566
Function: TIFFWritePerSampleShorts
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: _TIFFmalloc() is used to allocate an array when samples > 10, but its return value is not checked. If allocation fails, w remains NULL and is dereferenced in w[i] = v, causing a NULL pointer dereference.

